@@ -511,5 +515,4 @@
-      --  Legal values of CPU are the special Unspecified_CPU value which is
-      --  inserted by the compiler for tasks without CPU aspect, and those in
-      --  the range of CPU_Range but no greater than Number_Of_CPUs. Otherwise
-      --  the task is defined to have failed, and it becomes a completed task
-      --  (RM D.16(14/3)).
+      --  Native tasks retain the Ada limit of Number_Of_CPUs. For a
+      --  lightweight task, the CPU aspect selects an execution group instead
+      --  of a native processor, so values through CPU_Range'Last remain legal.
+      --  Other values make task creation fail as required by RM D.16(14/3).
@@ -516,3 +520,5 @@
-        and then (CPU < Integer (System.Multiprocessors.CPU_Range'First)
-                    or else
